    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you. When pain becomes the only constant, \"temporary\" can feel like a cruel joke, and the word \"fight\" can feel like a demand to keep bleeding. And yes, there is a kind of peace in letting go—but that peace shouldn't have to mean ending your story. You're not weak for wanting the struggle to stop; you're exhausted from carrying a weight that was never meant to be yours alone. Let someone help you carry it, even if it's just for one hour, one day—because the cycle can change, even if it doesn't feel possible right now.",
